    "id": "tradeoffs-02",
    "type": "concept",
    "tag": "tradeoff",
    "term": "Build vs buy",
    "prompt": "Say it out loud, then flip:",
    "sections": [
     [
      "Default",
      "“Buy, then build only the part that makes you different.” Off-the-shelf gets value in weeks, the vendor carries upgrades, and you learn where the real friction is."
     ],
     [
      "Build when all 3",
      "The workflow is core to how you win; it touches your systems and data in ways no product reaches; you’ll use it enough to justify owning it. Building = owning maintenance, security and model upgrades forever."
     ],
     [
      "Usually both",
      "Buy the platform, build a thin layer for the one or two workflows that matter most, like a claims agent that has to work inside a legacy system."
     ],
     [
      "The test",
      "“If a vendor shipped this next quarter, would we be annoyed or relieved?” Relieved → buy."
     ]
    ]
