    "id": "ai-06",
    "type": "concept",
    "tag": "ai",
    "term": "Human-in-the-loop thresholds",
    "sections": [
     [
      "What it is",
      "Rules for which actions an AI may take alone and which need a person to approve."
     ],
     [
      "Set by",
      "Reversibility and cost of a mistake. Draft, summarize, route: can run alone. Deny money, price risk, send, change a record, clinical guidance: a person approves."
     ],
     [
      "Confidence",
      "Below a confidence threshold, a human triages. Red-flag cases (e.g. an urgent symptom) always escalate."
     ],
     [
      "Earn autonomy",
      "Log every decision and track the override rate. Sustained low overrides on one action → let it run alone, keep spot-checking."
     ]
    ]
